From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:02:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvk: CUDA kernels on Blackwell: launch constants and texture
 handles

DLSS ran on an RTX 5090 (sm_120, SASS from the host-built cubin cache)
without errors but wrote a black image.  Small PTX kernels compiled by
NVIDIA's JIT for sm_120 and run through VK_NVX_binary_import
(ngx-smoketest --cutest) showed three differences from what NVK did,
which came from the Turing to Ada ABI:

- Bank 0 layout.  sm_100+ SASS has its parameters at 0x380 and reads
  %ntid from 0x360, %nctaid from 0x370, the initial stack pointer from
  0x37c and the generic address of the local memory window (cvta.local)
  from 0x2f8.  NVK wrote the block and grid sizes at 0x0 and 0xc, so
  every kernel saw blockDim = gridDim = 0 (pixel = blockIdx * 0 +
  threadIdx), and kernels with a stack frame put it below local address
  0, outside the thread's local memory, where loads return zero.  The
  launch now fills them: the stack starts at the top of the slm_size
  bytes the QMD gives each thread.  Before sm_100 the layout is as it was.

- Texture handles.  The texture instructions in this SASS take the whole
  handle as the texture header index; NVK's combined handle has the
  sampler index in bits 20-31, so a texture with any sampler but the one
  at index 0 read another (or no) header and returned zeros, fetches
  included.  The sampler comes from the QMD: CUDA launches on Blackwell
  now use SAMPLER_INDEX_VIA_HEADER_INDEX (new nak_qmd_info field), and
  vkGetImageViewHandleNVX / vkGetImageViewHandle64NVX for a combined
  image sampler return an index where the image table holds a copy of the
  view's sampled descriptor and the sampler table a copy of the sampler
  (nvk_descriptor_table_insert_pair; one per view and sampler state,
  freed with the view).  Sampled and storage image handles are unchanged.

With this, the cutest kernels all give the expected results (launch
constants, module globals and __constant__ data, the stack and generic
local addresses, shared memory, textures with two samplers, surfaces,
cp.async, ldmatrix, mma.sync), and DLSS 310.9.16 super resolution
(preset K, 1280x720 to 1920x1080) in ngx-smoketest upscales the input:
mean difference to a nearest upscale of the input 4-5 of 255, the
aliased lines resolved; 0.43 ms GPU per evaluation.
